WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
Thank you.

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.730
Well hello, everybody.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.870
My name is John Mulaney.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.740
It's very nice to be here, very
nice to be out of the house,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.470
at night in general for me.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.810
I actually quite drinking
a few months ago,

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.137
because, yeah thank you for your support,

00:00:15.137 --> 00:00:16.740
(audience laughing)

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.360
but what had happened was I got to a point

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.570
where I was blacking
out every time I drank,

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.150
and I went to talk to my doctor about it,

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.090
and he said that it wasn't
that I was drinking too much,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.680
it's just that after you have
a couple major blackouts,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.230
your brain will blackout easier
and easier automatically.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.530
So like, I could go to a bar,

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.060
and have like one or two beers,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.487
and my brain would be like,

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:42.573
"Okay, I see where this is headed.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.940
Why don't we just power down now,

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.100
and then get restarted
sometime tomorrow morning?"

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.560
It was always weird when I
would go out for the night,

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.070
with like some money, and then blackout,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.680
and wake up with no money.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.730
It was even weirder though,

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.900
when I would go out for
the night with some money,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.474
blackout, and wake up with more money.

00:01:03.474 --> 00:01:05.190
(audience laughing)

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.854
Because, that means that I earned money.

00:01:07.854 --> 00:01:09.564
(audience laughing)

00:01:09.564 --> 00:01:14.564
And, that means that I traded
goods, and or services.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.910
Which is scary, but sometimes
I'd almost be proud of it,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:24.360
I'd be like, "Wow, I turned $20 into $100.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.860
I am a financial wizard."

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.650
Like, I'd like to give
people money advice,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.940
but I don't know how that would go,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.570
they'd be like, "John, I'm
looking to get rich quick."

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.410
And I be like, "Well, have
you tried mixing daiquiris

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.655
with Ambien?"

00:01:36.655 --> 00:01:38.600
(audience laughing)

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.610
They're like, "Does that work?"

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.434
And, I'm like, "It didn't not work."

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.120
(audience laughing)

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.375
Stay home now, and I
watch "Law and Order".

00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:49.560
That is my favorite show.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.950
I realized "Law and Order"
was my favorite show,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.870
when I was in my fourth consecutive hour

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.463
of "Law and Order".

00:01:55.463 --> 00:01:57.020
I figured this better be my favorite,

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.723
otherwise I have a problem.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.200
Best thing about "Law and Order" though,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.520
is that the same things
happen on every episode.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.160
Every single episode, it's
like watch it next time,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.330
in the beginning of every "Law and Order",

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.230
when the detective are like
first interviewing witnesses

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.020
for the case, the people
they talk to always act

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.080
like it's no big deal to be questioned

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.240
by homicide detectives.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.290
They're very casual about it.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.260
There's been like double rape and murder,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.717
and they're talking to
some guy, who's just like,

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:28.173
"Tony Ramirez?

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.133
Yeah, I remember him.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.920
Use to work here Tuesdays, right?"

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.254
It's like, Dude, people have died!

00:02:37.254 --> 00:02:39.040
(audience laughing)

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.326
You can't stop unloading
crates for a few seconds?

00:02:43.326 --> 00:02:44.561
(audience laughing)

00:02:44.561 --> 00:02:47.561
(audience appaulds)

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:53.690
How often do you talk
to homicide detectives?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.920
And then, they'll let
some detail about case go

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.210
that they don't even realize is important.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.657
He'll be like, "Well, did
he say where he was going?'

00:03:01.657 --> 00:03:03.610
"I don't know, he said
somethin' about going

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.950
to the knife store."

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.463
Yeah, knife store.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.041
Knife store pertains to
the stabbing investigation.

00:03:11.041 --> 00:03:14.041
(audience laughing)

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.640
I grew up catholic.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.841
I had to go to catholic schools.

00:03:19.841 --> 00:03:24.360
We had, yeah sure, we
had Bible study class

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.270
in the school I went to.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.020
Every week Bible study class,

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.770
and one Bible story
I've always remembered,

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.740
is the story of King Solomon and the baby.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.480
I don't know if you
guys remember this one.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.120
King Solomon, he's the
wise king of Israel,

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.460
and two women bring him a baby,

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.350
and they say, "We both
claim that this is our baby.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.990
What are you gonna do?"

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.177
And Solomon says,

00:03:46.177 --> 00:03:50.870
"Well, we will cut the
baby down the middle."

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.607
And the first woman says, "Oh, okay."

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.497
And the other woman says,

00:03:56.497 --> 00:03:59.450
"No, don't cut the baby down the middle."

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.350
And Solomon says, "Ah-ha, congratulations,

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.937
you have proven yourself
to be the real mother."

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:07.921
A couple things with that,

00:04:07.921 --> 00:04:10.360
(audience laughing)

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.360
One, who is this first woman?

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.300
Yeah it's like, "Yeah,
cut the baby in half,

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.420
that sounds like a good idea."

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.010
Like what kind of awful
woman has just stolen a baby,

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.900
she's stole a baby,

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.687
and then at the first inquest she's like,

00:04:23.687 --> 00:04:25.030
"look I'll take what I can get.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.620
Can I get the legs?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.690
I'll take the legs, she
can have the top part."

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:34.340
She's so whacked out, she
calls the head "the top part".

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.290
Secondly, that he knew
it was the real mother,

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.623
'cause she knew not to cut a baby in half.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:46.230
Oh, I think most people would
come to that conclusion.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.850
Like if I was walking down the street,

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.330
and I saw someone about
to saw a child in half,

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.509
I'd be like, "Hey, why
don't you not do that?"

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:56.250
And they'd be like. "Oh,
you must be the father,

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.957
well congratulations."

00:04:57.957 --> 00:04:59.208
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:04:59.208 --> 00:05:00.458
I'm John Mulaney.

00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:01.429
(audience appaulds)

00:05:01.429 --> 00:05:02.262
Thank you.

00:05:03.568 --> 00:05:04.416
That's hilarious.

00:05:04.416 --> 00:05:06.423
Thank you.
Yeah, thank you, so much.

00:05:06.423 --> 00:05:08.040
Very funny John Mulaney.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:08.873
We'll take a break.

00:05:08.873 --> 00:05:09.706
We'll be right--

